<!--
  Für Elise
  Bagatelle No. 25 in A minor, WoO 59 (1810): the opening section. Ludwig van Beethoven.
  Public domain. A minor, 3/8, eighth = 120 (quarter = 60), pickup + 28 bars (43 s):
  the first part twice, the middle part, then the first part again.
  Melody (right hand) only, C4-F5, in the C4-B5 window. The left-hand arpeggios are left out,
  and the passage that leads back to the theme (a leap to E6, then E5 and D#5 in turn) is
  shortened to one bar (20).

  bar | right hand         | words
    0 | E5 D#5             |
    1 | E5 D#5 E5 B4 D5 C5 | first part
    2 | A4 C4 E4 A4        |
    3 | B4 E4 G#4 B4       |
    4 | C5 E4 E5 D#5       |
    5 | E5 D#5 E5 B4 D5 C5 |
    6 | A4 C4 E4 A4        |
    7 | B4 E4 C5 B4        |
    8 | A4 E5 D#5          | first ending
    9 | E5 D#5 E5 B4 D5 C5 | first part again
   10 | A4 C4 E4 A4        |
   11 | B4 E4 G#4 B4       |
   12 | C5 E4 E5 D#5       |
   13 | E5 D#5 E5 B4 D5 C5 |
   14 | A4 C4 E4 A4        |
   15 | B4 E4 C5 B4        |
   16 | A4 B4 C5 D5        | second ending
   17 | E5 G4 F5 E5        | middle part
   18 | D5 F4 E5 D5        |
   19 | C5 E4 D5 C5        |
   20 | B4 E4 E5 D#5       | link, shortened
   21 | E5 D#5 E5 B4 D5 C5 | first part
   22 | A4 C4 E4 A4        |
   23 | B4 E4 G#4 B4       |
   24 | C5 E4 E5 D#5       |
   25 | E5 D#5 E5 B4 D5 C5 |
   26 | A4 C4 E4 A4        |
   27 | B4 E4 C5 B4        |
   28 | A4                 |
-->
